Subject: Tweak: blue Peach
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Peach has a second kit on the disc, blue with yellow: peach_alt.rlt, her
goalie's peachgoalie_alt.rlt and her six sidekicks' <sidekick>_peach_alt.rlt
textures. CharacterLoader dresses a captain in his alternate kit against a
captain of his colours (GetAlternateCaptain, NeedsAlternateColour), but no
other captain shares Peach's colour, so the retail game never shows it.

With "Blue Peach" enabled, Peach's team wears it on the field:
HasAlternateSwapTexture swaps Peach's and her goalie's kit for it, her
sidekicks load their _alt team textures, and the player indicators and the
defensive play overlay take its colour (Peach's alternate colour). The game
has no blue version of her menu pictures, Mega Strike hand, stadium banners
or crowd, so those stay pink. In a match of Peach against herself (Mirror
match) the away team wears the blue kit, as without the tweak.

diff --git a/include/Game/DB/CharacterInfo.h b/include/Game/DB/CharacterInfo.h
index 3659959..67e0cdf 100644
--- a/include/Game/DB/CharacterInfo.h
+++ b/include/Game/DB/CharacterInfo.h
@@ -85,4 +85,11 @@ nlColour GetAwayKitColour(const CharacterInfo& team);
 bool HasWholeAwayKit(const CharacterInfo& captain);
 #endif
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// Port tweak "Blue Peach": Peach's team wears her blue kit on the field
+// (GetAwayKitColour is its team colour). Against herself (Mirror match) the
+// away team wears it, as without the tweak.
+bool BluePeachKit(const CharacterInfo& team, const CharacterInfo& opponent);
+#endif
+
 #endif // GAME_DB_CHARACTERINFO_H
diff --git a/src/Game/CharacterLoader.cpp b/src/Game/CharacterLoader.cpp
index 34ae4aa..5ee1bf5 100644
--- a/src/Game/CharacterLoader.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/CharacterLoader.cpp
@@ -193,6 +193,17 @@ static void MirrorMatchMakeAwayHand(eCharacterClass captain)
 }
 #endif
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// Port tweak "Blue Peach": Peach's team (captain, goalie and sidekicks) wears
+// her blue kit, the one the game would load against a captain of her colours.
+static bool BluePeachTeam(eCharacterClass captain0, eCharacterClass captain1, int team)
+{
+    const CharacterInfo& info0 = GetCharacterInfo(captain0);
+    const CharacterInfo& info1 = GetCharacterInfo(captain1);
+    return team == 0 ? BluePeachKit(info0, info1) : BluePeachKit(info1, info0);
+}
+#endif
